description_preview:
Glotman Simpson US Inc. is one of North America’s leading engineering firms, providing innovative solutions and unparalleled client service since 1964. For over 60 years, we’ve been providing quality, cost conscious structural engineering consulting services for more than 5,000 projects in the areas of high-rise residential, seismic upgrade, commercial, industrial and institutional buildings.
Our firm is currently looking for passionate
Junior-to-Senior Level Structural Design Engineers
to join our dynamic Los Angeles-based team. If you’re looking to expand your knowledge in a challenging technical environment, we’d like to hear from you! This is an exciting opportunity to develop your experience with a firm that offers excellent training to fit your current experience and to achieve your future goals.
Minimum Requirements:
·
3+ years of structural design experience;
·
Master’s degree with specialization in structural engineering;
·
Structural design experience in post-tensioned concrete, reinforced concrete, wood, masonry and steel;
·
Strong technical understanding of seismic design principles and structural dynamics;
·
A working knowledge of the California Building Code and relevant design standards (i.e. AISC, ACI, NDS);
·
Excellent verbal and written communication skills;
·
Ability to manage projects and deadlines;
·
P.E. license required, actively working towards S.E.
·
Ability to accurately read and interpret drawing plans.
And, you’re also described as being:
·
A difference-maker;
·
A positive team-player who is always seeking solutions to challenges;
·
Someone who communicates clearly and concisely;
·
A multi-tasker who thrives in a fast-paced environment;
·
Someone who radiates enthusiasm, energy and passion;
·
Someone who is organized, efficient and confident; and,
·
A critical thinker who manages ambiguity well and is able to identify the important questions.
If this sounds like you, here’s what you can expect to be doing as a Junior Level Structural Design Engineer:
·
Advancing your career by working on world class projects with mentorship from industry experts;
·
Creating plans, design, computer analysis, checking drawing reviews and calculations using engineering formulas and skills for design in accordance with established codes, standards, drawings, or other specifications;
·
Analyzing applicable reports, drawings, blueprints, tests, and related documentation to plan and design projects;
·
Using computer-assisted engineering and design software to prepare engineering and design documents and calculations;
·
Leading design coordination meetings with project consultants and clients;
·
Managing projects and project teams, assisting with training and development of younger engineers;
·
Conducting field reviews and structural observations; and,
·
Reviewing shop drawings, contractor requests and RFI’s.
If you can see yourself as part of our dynamic team, please send your resume + cover letter in PDF format to
careers@glotmansimpson.com
with “Structural Engineer Applicant – LA” in the subject line.
We appreciate all interest in our firm and will be in touch with you to request an interview if selected,
no phone calls please.
